            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Circulatory assistance is developing as a treatment for patients with end-stage heart failure. There are two alternative devices: a univentricular circulatory assist pump, or a total artificial heart. It is used to bridge the time to transplantation and, increasingly, as a definitive alternative to a heart transplant.</AbstractText>
